      "tree_id": "e144617e0434dc34d41b54da014ab317c0b364ab",
      "message": "3SUM issues run as split builds; PRs stay one job\n\nLead, 2026-11-02 (issue #99): the 3SUM proof of #99 compiled one module at a time for 5 h 16 min in one\njob (726 chains, 0 errors, 346 of 460 data batches) and ran out of time before the kernel check. The\nsplit profile builds the solution in job 1 with one parallel lake build, and job 2 restores it.\n\n- profiles/direct.json: 3sum gets \"runner\": \"github-split\". Its issues get split: true in the matrix.\n- The PR route has no build job and never splits. pr_submissions now refuses only problems outside its\n  folders (PR_PROBLEMS: dft, 3sum, apsp), not split profiles, so a 3SUM PR is still selected and runs in\n  pr_verify, as before.\n- verifier.chain_targets takes the split flag of the run (BOS_SPLIT, set by both issue jobs of\n  submission-check.yml) instead of the profile runner: a 3SUM PR keeps the one-module-at-a-time chain\n  build. A split flag on a profile without the split runner is refused.\n- docs/execution.md and tests (runner values, matrix entry, chain targets, a 3SUM PR is selected, the\n  BOS_SPLIT job env).\n\nThe receipt carries the profile, so the site import must accept the runner key before this lands\n(site commit with the trust entry for this revision).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
